{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1474391-submission-types","id":1474391,"title":"Submission Types?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-10T13:30:03-08:00","id":1474391,"title":"Submission Types?","content":"I am working on a writing submission for OPP. The requirements read &quot;We\u2019re looking for <i>new </i>submissions no longer than 1,000 words: 500 words of setting or fiction and 500 words of mechanics.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I am wondering, do you think NPC write up qould qualify? It would have a balance of mechanics and setting fiction.<br /> <br /> Come to that, how do you define &quot;setting fiction,&quot; as compared to mechanics?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T16:32:41-08:00","id":1474399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1474391-submission-types#post1474391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am working on a writing submission for OPP. The requirements read &quot;We\u2019re looking for <i>new </i>submissions no longer than 1,000 words: 500 words of setting or fiction and 500 words of mechanics.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I am wondering, do you think NPC write up qould qualify? It would have a balance of mechanics and setting fiction.<br /> <br /> Come to that, how do you define &quot;setting fiction,&quot; as compared to mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;500 words of setting <u>or</u> fiction&quot; and &quot;setting fiction,&quot; are two different types of criteria. Either/or gives you more freedom. Setting fiction sounds more like a description of a city with short historic entries pertaining to influential NPCs. <br /> <br /> That aside, if you are really inspired to develop a single character in detail, put him/her in a small city that you can read up on or already know well. It could be something like, &quot;City officials are trying to get approval to tear down a historic fort to make room for a housing development, but are meeting resistance from a litigious Heritage Society.&quot;. It could be an old Vampire, a Hermetic Mage or a Changeling defending an Estate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}